63\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#111\">Copy and complete the branch probabilities.</text></svg>"
    },
    {
      "number": 10,
      "section": "B",
      "marks": 15,
      "stem": "Let $f(x)=e^{x/5}$. A rectangle has vertices $(a,0)$, $(10,0)$, $(10,f(a))$ and $(a,f(a))$, where $0<a<10$. Its area is $S$ and perimeter is $P$.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "Find the equation of the tangent to the graph of $f$ at $x=0$.",
          "marks": 3
        },
        {
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "Show that $S=(10-a)e^{a/5}$.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "c",
          "prompt": "Write an expression for $P$ in terms of $a$.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "d",
          "prompt": "Find $\\mathrm{d}S/\\mathrm{d}a$.",
          "marks": 3
        },
        {
          "label": "e",
          "prompt": "Find the perimeter of the rectangle whose area is greatest. Justify that its area is a maximum.",
          "marks": 5
        }
      ],
      "answerSummary": "Tangent $y=x/5+1$; $S=(10-a)e^{a/5}$; maximum at $a=5$, with $P=10+2e$.",
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Differentiate $f$: $f\\,\\!\\prime(x)=e^{x/5}/5$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "The point is $(0,1)$ and the gradient is $1/5$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$y=x/5+1$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "The base is $10-a$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "The height is $e^{a/5}$, giving the stated product."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "c",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$P=2(10-a)+2e^{a/5}$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$P=20-2a+2e^{a/5}$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "d",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Apply the product rule."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{d}S/\\mathrm{d}a=-e^{a/5}+(10-a)e^{a/5}/5$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{d}S/\\mathrm{d}a=e^{a/5}-(a/5)e^{a/5}$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "e",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Set $\\mathrm{d}S/\\mathrm{d}a=0$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$e^{a/5}>0$, so $1-a/5=0$ and $a=5$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$S\\,\\!\\prime\\prime(a)=-(a/25)e^{a/5}$."
            },
            {
              "code": "R1",
              "text": "This is negative at 5; also $S\\,\\!\\prime$ changes from positive to negative on $(0,10)$, so this is the global maximum."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$P=10+2e$."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sourcePages": [
